---
title: Example · Checkout quality
config:
  look: classic
  theme: dark
  themeVariables:
    cScale0: "#b3b3b3"
    cScale1: "#93c5fd"
  themeCSS: |
    /* filled graticule rings wash out the curves */
    .radarGraticule { fill: none; stroke: #555555; }
    .radarCurve-0, .radarCurve-1 { fill-opacity: 0.1; }
---
%% `axis id["Label"]` per dimension, several per line; `curve id["Label"]{v, …}` lists values in axis order, `{axis: v, …}` names them.
%% `max`/`min` fix the scale, `ticks` sets ring count, `graticule polygon|circle` picks the rings, `showLegend false` hides the legend.
%% A body `title …` line is the alternative to frontmatter `title`.
%% `config.radar`: `width` · `height` · `marginTop` … · `axisScaleFactor` · `axisLabelFactor` · `curveTension`.
radar-beta
  axis perf["Performance"], rel["Reliability"], ux["Usability"]
  axis sec["Security"], cost["Cost"]
  curve now["Current"]{3, 4, 2, 4, 3}
  curve target["Target"]{ cost: 3, perf: 4, rel: 5, ux: 4, sec: 5 }
  showLegend true
  max 5
  min 0
  ticks 5
  graticule polygon
